[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186124562 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/id #uuid "2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-102805" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation $x{y}^{″}-(x+1){y}^{′}+y=0$ for $x>0.$ Use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x)\\cdot {e}^{x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{x}$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{x}+2{u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({u}^{″}{e}^{x}+2{u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x})-(x+1)({u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x})+u{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+2{u}^{′}x+ux)-{e}^{x}{u}^{′}(x+1)-{e}^{x}u(x+1)+{e}^{x}u & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+2{u}^{′}x+ux-{u}^{′}(x+1)-u(x+1)+u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(2x-x-1)+u(x-x-1+1)) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(x-1)) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}\\ne 0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(x-1)=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}x+w(x-1)=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}x{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}x{e}^{-x}\\,⟹\\,u=-{c}_{1}(1+x){e}^{-x}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{x}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}(-{c}_{1}(1+x){e}^{-x}+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=(1+x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" "answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" "answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" "answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/id #uuid "e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1+x){e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/id #uuid "28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1+{x}^{2}){e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/id #uuid "91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/id #uuid "77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/id #uuid "f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/id #uuid "6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/math-academy-id "q-86452" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,{e}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-1,{e}^{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\text{ }i-2yz\\text{ }j-{y}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-1,{e}^{2}) & =2{e}^{2}\\text{ }i-2(-1)({e}^{2})\\text{ }j-(-1)^{2}k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{2}\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,{e}^{2})\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" "answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" "answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" "answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/id #uuid "40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},-1,2{e}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/id #uuid "7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/id #uuid "45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/id #uuid "5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/id #uuid "9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124497 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/id #uuid "af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37159" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/id #uuid "79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" "answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" "answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" "answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/id #uuid "9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/id #uuid "8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/id #uuid "21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/id #uuid "f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/id #uuid "c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119841 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/id #uuid "39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33453" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,-8,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $2x+y-2z=-7.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=-3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-7 \\\\ 2(1)+(-3)+7 & =2z \\\\ 6 & =2z \\\\ z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,-3,3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-3,3⟩-⟨-2,-8,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+5-8|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,3\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" "answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" "answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" "answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/id #uuid "d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/id #uuid "4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/id #uuid "3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/id #uuid "6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/id #uuid "71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119794 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/id #uuid "39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75094" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-4,{u}_{23}=3,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=-12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" "answer-ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" "answer-70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" "answer-d29b0f99-07ab-51ab-98fe-551c80011b17" "answer-7cf259a9-c7cf-53af-a02f-d46c56183bb5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer/id #uuid "2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" :answer/id #uuid "ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" :answer/id #uuid "70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d29b0f99-07ab-51ab-98fe-551c80011b17" :answer/id #uuid "d29b0f99-07ab-51ab-98fe-551c80011b17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cf259a9-c7cf-53af-a02f-d46c56183bb5" :answer/id #uuid "7cf259a9-c7cf-53af-a02f-d46c56183bb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-bacf2968-3b49-5c21-b368-bdf573fb3974" :activity/id #uuid "bacf2968-3b49-5c21-b368-bdf573fb3974" :activity/title "Quiz 5" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-a2394cb1-b097-5e37-a7b2-465f90ba6189" "step-53334c82-cc45-5add-b5ff-772f81592394" "step-c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" "step-d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" "step-eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" "step-dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa"] :activity/first-step "step-a2394cb1-b097-5e37-a7b2-465f90ba6189" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a2394cb1-b097-5e37-a7b2-465f90ba6189" :step/id #uuid "a2394cb1-b097-5e37-a7b2-465f90ba6189" :step/content "question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :step/next "step-53334c82-cc45-5add-b5ff-772f81592394" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-53334c82-cc45-5add-b5ff-772f81592394" :step/id #uuid "53334c82-cc45-5add-b5ff-772f81592394" :step/content "question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :step/next "step-c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" :step/id #uuid "c4ff6dfe-8366-5d8d-bc78-c185c460c2ab" :step/content "question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :step/next "step-d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" :step/id #uuid "d7639e75-43c0-5601-a994-c8254e1991b7" :step/content "question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :step/next "step-eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" :step/id #uuid "eb60143a-1a6f-5876-85ba-046c11dcc560" :step/content 17592186351282 :step/next "step-dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa" :step/id #uuid "dd9d7097-e295-58a1-bbd5-ff75664f3faa" :step/content "question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/id #uuid "2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2"] ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-102805"] ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/problem "The function ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation $x{y}^{″}-(x+1){y}^{′}+y=0$ for $x>0.$ Use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation."] ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x)\\cdot {e}^{x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{x}$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{x}+2{u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x({u}^{″}{e}^{x}+2{u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x})-(x+1)({u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x})+u{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+2{u}^{′}x+ux)-{e}^{x}{u}^{′}(x+1)-{e}^{x}u(x+1)+{e}^{x}u & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+2{u}^{′}x+ux-{u}^{′}(x+1)-u(x+1)+u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(2x-x-1)+u(x-x-1+1)) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(x-1)) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}\\ne 0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}(x-1)=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}x+w(x-1)=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}x{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}x{e}^{-x}\\,⟹\\,u=-{c}_{1}(1+x){e}^{-x}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{x}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}(-{c}_{1}(1+x){e}^{-x}+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=(1+x).\n$$"] ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897"] ["answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/id #uuid "e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3"] ["answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3" :answer/value "(1+x){e}^{-x}"] ["answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/id #uuid "28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154"] ["answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154" :answer/value "(1+{x}^{2}){e}^{x}"] ["answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/id #uuid "91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054"] ["answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054" :answer/value "1+x"] ["answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/id #uuid "77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873"] ["answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873" :answer/value "1+{x}^{2}"] ["answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/id #uuid "f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4"] ["answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4" :answer/value "x{e}^{x}"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/correct "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/choices "answer-e35d38c6-3fdf-5442-8857-924d4b6cc5c3"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/choices "answer-28c0b99d-78d6-5231-ab0c-4e7bd6097154"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/choices "answer-91d12be6-febe-58af-a555-4e143641e054"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/choices "answer-77536e08-1521-58eb-b267-67f914b8d873"] ["answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897" :answer-field/choices "answer-f50f4556-c1f6-54c3-a55b-86f88caf8fd4"] ["question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f1e8ec1f-41ee-5320-b7b5-0129ea48c897"] [17592186124562 :knowledge-point/questions "question-2abfd6a6-feff-503c-bea4-5ba5b90fc5a2"] ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/id #uuid "6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677"] ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/math-academy-id "q-86452"] ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,{e}^{2}).$"] ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-1,{e}^{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{2x}-{y}^{2}z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\text{ }i-2yz\\text{ }j-{y}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-1,{e}^{2}) & =2{e}^{2}\\text{ }i-2(-1)({e}^{2})\\text{ }j-(-1)^{2}k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}\\,i+2{e}^{2}\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,{e}^{2})\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec"] ["answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/id #uuid "40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242"] ["answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242" :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},-1,2{e}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-e⟩=0"] ["answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/id #uuid "7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc"] ["answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc" :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0"] ["answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/id #uuid "45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f"] ["answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f" :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0"] ["answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/id #uuid "5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c"] ["answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c" :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0"] ["answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/id #uuid "9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc"] ["answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc" :answer/value "⟨2{e}^{2},2{e}^{2},1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-{e}^{2}⟩=0"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/correct "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/choices "answer-40caae58-4e1d-5f93-b1ec-cd75d7157242"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/choices "answer-7e549ac3-36d9-54ef-9d4f-2d2e265336cc"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/choices "answer-45f9c210-ee79-5f2b-a8eb-4524c18c870f"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/choices "answer-5b51d704-e920-5228-82c9-0cddcfcd5d3c"] ["answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec" :answer-field/choices "answer-9722fb6a-0bb9-510c-95ed-2158bd8babfc"] ["question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-69e14aac-1ab9-5ef1-86cb-e05f2514d2ec"] [17592186129079 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6a99613e-1f33-5aa3-a707-361661349677"] ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/id #uuid "af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e"] ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37159"] ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the standard basis $S$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$"] ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change-of-coordinates formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/id #uuid "79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da"] ["answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/id #uuid "9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9"] ["answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/id #uuid "8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c"] ["answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/id #uuid "21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096"] ["answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/id #uuid "f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d"] ["answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/id #uuid "c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636"] ["answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636" :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/correct "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/choices "answer-9c971210-23ba-5a3d-9d48-b48f9a6fc7d9"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/choices "answer-8a8f88fa-1943-5b66-9a8b-582f194c3e5c"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/choices "answer-21856be1-b1fa-5f91-8a39-4aebb5209096"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/choices "answer-f5a9c01f-6c85-52fc-b668-f80c2e6a714d"] ["answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da" :answer-field/choices "answer-c0c1e9fb-4917-514f-8d69-f634fa62d636"] ["question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-79a8ed53-1004-51ec-854e-1bc8377232da"] [17592186124497 :knowledge-point/questions "question-af173c80-5734-52f5-887a-4f2d2e37a60e"] ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/id #uuid "39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5"] ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33453"] ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,-8,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $2x+y-2z=-7.$"] ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=-3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-7 \\\\ 2(1)+(-3)+7 & =2z \\\\ 6 & =2z \\\\ z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,-3,3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-3,3⟩-⟨-2,-8,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,5,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6+5-8|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,3\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987"] ["answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/id #uuid "d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37"] ["answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/id #uuid "4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04"] ["answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/id #uuid "3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7"] ["answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/id #uuid "6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f"] ["answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/id #uuid "71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db"] ["answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db" :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/correct "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/choices "answer-d2870e0f-6294-5f82-8056-6334f7ab8f37"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/choices "answer-4738641c-2dc2-53da-9d9a-b5f351c18c04"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/choices "answer-3e48c6e1-979b-5319-ab3b-cf3af3e4ddf7"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/choices "answer-6020578e-6c29-5a90-8cfa-60aa1062193f"] ["answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987" :answer-field/choices "answer-71da091c-aca1-5ad0-8e35-00a66ee352db"] ["question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b4a98275-e739-51cc-8112-6d634db0f987"] [17592186119841 :knowledge-point/questions "question-39c46748-4786-53ad-a218-6f5fdd2db8c5"] ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/id #uuid "39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9"] ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75094"] ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=$"] ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-4,{u}_{23}=3,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{23}=-12.$"] ["question-39a7d310-9046-5578-9f8d-31308eeefed9" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e485ffe4-c9b3-59e1-9725-0e402d6b690f"] ["answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer/id #uuid "2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee"] ["answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2e7f22e7-8655-56ca-99a2-efa5c63acdee" :answer/value "-12"] ["answer-ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" :answer/id #uuid "ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d"] ["answer-ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ec561c11-e653-5aca-ba10-c9323edae82d" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" :answer/id #uuid "70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f"] ["answer-70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-70be245a-94da-5521-81f7-b1eff4563a5f" :answer/value "-8"] ["answer-d29b0f99-07ab-51ab-98fe-551c80011b17" :answer/id #uuid "d29b0f99-07ab-51ab-98fe-551c80011b17"] ["answer-d29b